ntence both in terms of the  sentence embedding and word similarity  so these were the metrics that we stuck  with for how to train a good  conversation model  and so basically what we wanted to do is  use reinforcement learning to actually  learn to optimize these metrics  by putting our bots on the web and  having them interact with humans so  basically instead of your normal rl  paradigm where the agent is interacting  with a simulated environment in our  paradigm the agent is actually  interacting with a human a human is the  environment that's providing rewards  based on whether they enjoyed the  conversation  um  but wait did i just say i wanted to put  an agent online and have it interact  with humans on the internet to teach it  how to talk  i think we've seen how badly that can go  in the past so  we decided in the context of this  project that we actually needed to  carefully test any model that we trained  offline before deploying it back to  human so we can't have it learning  online from interacting with humans  about how to talk  and so what this necessitated is  actually to do  uh  fully offline learning which means that  our normal interaction or exploration  part of the rl loop is broken um so  instead of being able to explore to find  which actions lead to high payoff we  have to learn entirely offline so we're  in this off policy from static data  batch or offline rl setting this is a  very challenging setting because a lot  of rl algorithms are built such that um  they're optimistic in the face of  uncertainty and the exploration is  actually key to refining the estimates  that they learn  so  i'll give you a quick illustration of  why offline rl is hard so let's say  you're this little robot and you're  trying to learn to walk to this red flag  but you're only given the data in a  single batch of data and the probability  that your c a state in the batch is  shown in yellow here so basically  anything in this region that's white off  of this yel